35,2,1,talk,May,,"The old pilots worked. The audits say waiting is the real killer, not ticketing.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,The late-turn pool is empty. We are running on overtime. This is a crisis.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Midori,,"The data confirms my fear. The surface route is slow, but platforms clear fine. The issue is connections.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"I found that the ferry and rail data systems are incompatible. Also, old station work is risky and expensive due to hidden voids.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,The capital ledger is tight. Ticketing fees are eating our paving budget. We can’t afford to ignore the long-term drain.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,May,,"@Midori, so if we fix connections, we fix the journey.","{""words"":10,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Shizue, if the station work is that risky, maybe we should avoid it?","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Benjamin, the station upgrades might be necessary, but the data suggests the bus corridor could help with the surface slowness.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shizue,,The station upgrades are dangerous. The data mismatch makes a unified fare system hard.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"The ticketing fees are a leak. A unified system might stop that, but the capital is gone.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,May,,The night service pilot was a success. Maybe we should extend that?,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@May, we don’t have the crews for night service. The roster books are red.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Midori,,"The bus corridor addresses the surface slowness. The station upgrades address the access, but the risk is high.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shizue,,I am leaning away from the station upgrades. The hidden costs are too high.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"I am concerned about the ticketing fees. A unified platform might save money long-term, but the capital is tight.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,May,,Let’s vote for the plan that fixes the biggest pain point without breaking the bank or the crews.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,I cannot support any plan that ignores the staffing crisis.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Midori,,The bus corridor seems the most viable. It addresses the surface slowness directly.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shizue,,I agree with Midori. The station work is too risky. The bus corridor is safer.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,I will support the plan that stops the financial leak. The ticketing fees are unsustainable.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
