60,3,1,talk,May,,The audits show waiting is the problem. The bus corridor helps with surface speed. The fare platform helps with the leak.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,I am stuck. The bus corridor needs crews we don’t have. The fare platform needs capital we don’t have.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Midori,,The bus corridor directly addresses the timed run slowness. It’s the most direct fix for the passenger experience.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shizue,,The station upgrades are out. The night service is out due to staffing. It’s between A and B.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,The ticketing fees are a major drain. Option A stops that. But the capital is tight.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,May,,"@Benjamin, the bus corridor uses existing bus crews, not the late-turn pool.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@May, the roadway crews are a third below establishment. Who maintains the dedicated lanes?","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Midori,,"The maintenance contract for lifts has spare capacity, but the roadway crews are thin. This is a risk.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shizue,,The roadway consents are delegated to us. That helps. But the crew shortage is real.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"The ticketing fees are an annual drain. The bus corridor is a one-off capital cost, but the capital is ring-fenced.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,May,,The old pilots show the fare system works. The audits show the bus corridor helps. I’m torn.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,I cannot vote for a plan that ignores the crew shortage. But I also can’t ignore the financial leak.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Midori,,I will vote for the bus corridor. It fixes the most visible problem for passengers.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shizue,,I will vote for the bus corridor. It is less risky than the station work and addresses the surface slowness.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,I will vote for the fare platform. The financial leak is unsustainable. We must stop the bleeding.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,May,,I will vote for the bus corridor. It’s the most direct fix for the journey time.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,"I will vote for the fare platform. It’s the only way to stop the financial drain, even if the capital is tight.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Midori,,I will vote for the bus corridor.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Shizue,,I will vote for the bus corridor.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,I will vote for the fare platform.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
